All confirmed plain, no special setup. Both direct dependencies of `rt-fi` — `com.sun.xml.ws:jaxws-rt` (the relocated `rt` artifact) and `com.sun.xml.fastinfoset:FastInfoset` — already have metadata in this repo, and their own test scaffolds are plain unit tests with no Docker, no extra Maven deps, and no env/system properties. `rt-fi` itself is a tiny 8-class module (SOAP 1.1/1.2 Fast Infoset codecs) whose only two dependencies are declared as regular (non-optional) compile-scope deps in its POM, so Gradle's normal transitive resolution from `testImplementation "com.sun.xml.ws:rt-fi:$libraryVersion"` already pulls in everything needed. It performs pure in-memory XML/SOAP encoding — no network, filesystem, or external service involved.

